3. Temporary Conversation Memory

To maintain conversational context, Uni-Chan Thorium stores recent conversations in temporary memory.

Temporary memory:

Exists only while the Bot is running.
Is not intended as permanent storage.
Is automatically cleared when the Bot restarts.
May be manually cleared through available commands.

This temporary storage is used solely to improve conversation quality and continuity.

4. AI Training and Learning

Uni-Chan Thorium is a learning project and may use approved information to improve future versions of the model.

Training Data Usage

Ordinary conversations are not automatically added to permanent training datasets solely because a user interacts with the Bot.

Training data may only be created through:

Explicit user approval.
Administrator-approved training workflows.
Training review processes.
Dedicated training commands.
Approved Examples

When approved for training, examples may include:

User prompts
Assistant responses
Revised responses
Evaluation feedback
Coaching examples

Approved examples may be added to supervised learning datasets used for future model training.

5. NVIDIA Evaluation Services

When configured by the Bot owner, Uni-Chan Thorium may use NVIDIA AI services to evaluate generated responses.

When NVIDIA evaluation is enabled:

User prompts may be sent to NVIDIA.
AI responses may be sent to NVIDIA.
NVIDIA may provide ratings, evaluations, or coaching suggestions.

These services are used to:

Evaluate response quality.
Improve generated responses.
Assist with training workflows.

If NVIDIA services are not enabled, evaluation remains local.

Users should assume that prompts and generated responses may be transmitted to NVIDIA whenever NVIDIA-based evaluation features are active.

6. User Ratings

The Bot may request voluntary ratings for generated responses.

Stored rating data may include:

User ID
Rating value
Message identifiers
Channel identifiers
Server identifiers
Timestamp
Model version

Ratings are used for:

Measuring performance
Improving future versions
Evaluating response quality

Rating records do not necessarily contain message content.

7. Saved Conversations

By default, conversation content is not permanently archived.

Permanent storage occurs only when:

A user chooses to save conversation data.
A training workflow requires an approved example.
An administrator initiates a save operation.
A coaching workflow explicitly creates a training example.

Saved records may contain:

User prompts
Assistant responses
Evaluation notes
Training metadata
8. Data Sharing

Uni-Chan Thorium does not sell personal information.

Information may only be shared:

With NVIDIA evaluation services when enabled.
When required by law.
To investigate abuse or security issues.
With user permission.
When necessary to operate the service.
9. Data Security

Reasonable steps are taken to protect stored information, including:

Local storage controls
Access restrictions
Protected configuration files
Security-conscious development practices

However, no system can guarantee absolute security.

10. User Rights

Users may request:

Information regarding stored data.
Deletion of eligible records.
Removal of approved training examples when technically feasible.
Withdrawal of future training consent.
Deletion of saved conversations attributable to them.

Requests should be directed to the Bot owner or server administrators.

11. Children's Privacy

Uni-Chan Thorium is not intended for users below the minimum age required by Discord and applicable laws.

12. Experimental AI Disclaimer

Uni-Chan Thorium is an experimental AI system.

Users acknowledge that:

Responses may be incorrect.
Responses may contain factual errors.
Responses should not be relied upon for medical, legal, financial, or safety-critical decisions.
Training methods, datasets, and system behavior may change over time.
13. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated periodically.

Continued use of Uni-Chan Thorium following any changes constitutes acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.

14. Contact

Questions regarding this Privacy Policy should be directed to the owner or administrator of Uni-Chan Thorium.

Consent Notice

By interacting with Uni-Chan Thorium, you acknowledge that:

Temporary conversation data may be processed to generate responses.
Feedback and ratings may be stored if submitted.
Prompts and responses may be sent to NVIDIA when NVIDIA evaluation features are enabled.
Training data is only created through designated approval, review, or training workflows.
The project is experimental and continuously evolving.

